    "background_story": "Dr. Allan was a renowned paleontologist with a passion for ancient reptiles. His life's work focused on the Anapsida, a group of primitive reptiles that dominated Earth's landscapes during the Paleozoic era. Allan spent years studying the fossil records, searching for clues about the evolution and behavior of these enigmatic creatures. His groundbreaking research led to the discovery of a new Anapsid species, which he named 'Cryptanapsis allani' in honor of his mentor. Allan's work shed new light on the biology and diversity of Anapsids, earning him the prestigious Golden Trilobite award. His dedication to the field inspired a new generation of paleontologists, and his name became synonymous with Anapsid expertise.",
